messages:
maria_support: Hey team — customer reports sporadic 502s and says they can't find any request/trace id to share. I asked them for a minimal repro but want a single concise checklist to send. keeping it short for the customer.

maria_support: Hi @customer_acme — can you please run one of the following and paste the entire result (do NOT redact the request id / debug token). Also tell us the local time (and timezone) when the failure happened.

maria_support: 1) Easiest: open your browser devtools -> Network -> find the failing request -> right-click -> Copy -> "Copy as cURL" and paste here. We only need the single failing request.

maria_support: 2) If curl is easier, run:
```bash
curl -v -X POST https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate \\  -H 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_KEY>' \\  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\  -d '{"input":"hello"}'
```
Include the full terminal output (headers + body). Look for a response header called `x-redwood-request-id` or `x-request-id` in the response. Copy that value here.

maria_support: 3) If you're using our SDK, please paste the short snippet that reproduces it and add one line to log the response headers: e.g. Node/JS: 
```js
const res = await client.generate(...);
console.log('resp-headers', res.headers || res._rawHeaders || res.meta?.responseHeaders);
// or if error:
console.error(err.meta?.request_id || err.response?.headers['x-request-id']);
```
This usually surfaces `x-redwood-request-id` or `request_id` in error meta.

maria_support: Mobile apps: for Android (OkHttp) add a tiny interceptor to log response headers:
```java
new Interceptor() {
  public Response intercept(Chain chain) throws IOException {
    Response r = chain.proceed(chain.request());
    String rid = r.header("x-redwood-request-id");
    Log.i("REDWOOD-RID", rid + " status=" + r.code());
    return r;
  }
};
```

maria_support: If they cannot give a request id, ask for a HAR export. Steps: DevTools -> Network -> right click -> Save all as HAR with content. Attach the .har file (can be large).

maria_support: Quick note on debug-token: if we need deeper traces, ask them to generate a debug token from Console > Project > Support > Create debug snapshot (or paste client SDK command `await client.debug.createSnapshot()` if using SDK). The debug token looks like `dbg_<alphanumeric>` — paste that token, not the whole snapshot URL.

maria_support: Please also include: timestamp (ISO), region (e.g., us-west1), route/model name (if known), and approximate payload size.

maria_support: Security note: redact user PII from body but keep any IDs, request headers, and the debug token intact.

julian_eng: +1. Also ask them to capture one successful request (if possible) around the same time so we can diff headers/prefix.

priya_support: Add: if they run curl, include `--include` or `-i` so response headers are shown. Example: `curl -i -X POST ...`

maria_support: good call. I'll send this checklist to the customer now.

infra-bot: Internal doc: https://internal.redwood/docs/support/repro-checklist — contains the exact header names and example parsers (for us).

maria_support: thanks. If they paste the cURL or debug token here I will attach it to the ticket and escalate to eng with the RID.

julian_eng: if they give a RID and we still can't find it, ask for the proxied timestamp (client clock) + server time — that lets us search logs across regions quickly.

priya_support: I'll follow up if they reply with a HAR or token. :thumbsup:
